WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.932
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:14.996
Unit ten: Writing an Opinion Paragraph. Today you will give your opinion with reasons.

4
00:00:15.296 --> 00:00:17.937
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.121
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:23.868
Opinion.

7
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:27.092
Opinion means what you think about something.

8
00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:28.917
Give your opinion.

9
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:32.088
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

10
00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:35.818
Opinion.

11
00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:37.457
Agree.

12
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.531
Agree means to have the same view.

13
00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:42.629
I agree with this idea.

14
00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:45.753
Your turn. Say: Agree.

15
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.543
Agree.

16
00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.075
Believe.

17
00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:54.350
Believe means to think something is true.

18
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.996
I believe schools should start later.

19
00:00:57.583 --> 00:00:59.957
Your turn. Say: Believe.

20
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.580
Believe.

21
00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:05.062
Reason.

22
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.108
Reason means why you think something.

23
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:10.182
Give two reasons.

24
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:13.238
Your turn. Say: Reason.

25
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.031
Reason.

26
00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:18.541
Firmly.

27
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.387
Firmly means in a strong way.

28
00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:23.646
I firmly believe this.

29
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.728
Your turn. Say: Firmly.

30
00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:30.452
Firmly.

31
00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:32.160
Support.

32
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.602
Support means to give proof for an idea.

33
00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:37.740
Support your opinion.

34
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.933
Your turn. Say: Support.

35
00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:44.628
Support.

36
00:01:45.383 --> 00:01:46.373
Obviously.

37
00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:50.010
Obviously means in a way that is easy to see.

38
00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:52.802
Obviously, exercise helps.

39
00:01:53.417 --> 00:01:56.324
Your turn. Say: Obviously.

40
00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:00.539
Obviously.

41
00:02:01.283 --> 00:02:02.064
Conclude.

42
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.584
Conclude means to end with a final point.

43
00:02:06.183 --> 00:02:08.078
I conclude that it is useful.

44
00:02:08.683 --> 00:02:11.208
Your turn. Say: Conclude.

45
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:14.963
Conclude.

46
00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:19.777
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.617 --> 00:02:22.639
Visal, how do I write my opinion?

48
00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:31.827
State your opinion in the first sentence. For example, I believe students should learn to cook. Then give reasons.

49
00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:34.266
How many reasons?

50
00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:41.567
Give two or three, each with an example. Reasons make the opinion strong and fair.

51
00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:43.907
How do I finish?

52
00:02:45.017 --> 00:02:52.510
Restate your opinion in different words. For example, In conclusion, cooking is a valuable skill for every student.

53
00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.202
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:59.013
Grammar focus: Opinion phrases.

55
00:02:59.313 --> 00:03:00.616
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:01.317 --> 00:03:03.548
I believe that students should learn to cook.

57
00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.135
In my opinion, sport is good for everyone.

58
00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:13.641
Use I believe that or In my opinion to introduce your view, then support it with reasons and examples.

59
00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:17.814
Be careful! Don't say: I am agree with this.

60
00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.778
Say: I agree with this.

61
00:03:22.078 --> 00:03:23.694
Do not use am with agree.

62
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.955
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.232
Should Students Cook?.

64
00:03:29.532 --> 00:03:32.205
Sambath believes that students should learn to cook.

65
00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.710
His first reason is that cooking saves money.

66
00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:39.535
His second reason is that home food is healthier.

67
00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:42.753
He gives an example from his own life.

68
00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:46.637
In conclusion, cooking is a valuable skill.

69
00:03:47.733 --> 00:03:51.364
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:52.217 --> 00:03:53.961
An opinion is what you blank.

71
00:03:54.261 --> 00:03:57.136
A, eat. B, think. C, own.

72
00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.247
The answer is B: think.

73
00:04:03.383 --> 00:04:05.081
Reasons blank an opinion.

74
00:04:05.381 --> 00:04:08.663
A, stop. B, hide. C, support.

75
00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.188
The answer is C: support.

76
00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.512
In my opinion introduces a blank.

77
00:04:17.812 --> 00:04:20.664
A, view. B, date. C, name.

78
00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.246
The answer is A: view.

79
00:04:27.383 --> 00:04:29.453
The last sentence blank the opinion.

80
00:04:29.753 --> 00:04:33.685
A, denies. B, restates. C, forgets.

81
00:04:37.233 --> 00:04:39.326
The answer is B: restates.

82
00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:42.785
Sambath says cooking saves blank.

83
00:04:43.085 --> 00:04:46.843
A, time only. B, water. C, money.

84
00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.400
The answer is C: money.

85
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.775
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:04:57.617 --> 00:04:59.639
How do you write an opinion paragraph?

87
00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.985
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:10.285 --> 00:05:21.404
I state my opinion clearly with I believe that. Then I give two or three reasons and an example for each. I finish by restating my opinion in a conclusion.

89
00:05:21.704 --> 00:05:23.413
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:24.317 --> 00:05:28.467
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and opinion phrases.

91
00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:33.671
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

92
00:05:33.971 --> 00:05:36.635
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

93
00:05:36.935 --> 00:05:39.762
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

